1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Does posting twice today cost you 40% of your reach?
For You Skills checks the recommendation code.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,500
A different topic is ready. Should you publish today?
Yes, if it is ready and useful to your readers.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:15,000
That is editorial advice. This code does not establish
a daily quota or a guaranteed best posting time.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,500
The function counts candidates by the same author,
ordered by score within this ranking call.

5
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:26,000
Each call starts a fresh count. There is no daily
counter or four-hour reset in this function.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,500
With author diversity enabled and these published
defaults, the second candidate gets a 0.625 multiplier.

7
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:39,000
This changes a score; it does not predict impressions.
Your newest post could be the highest-scoring candidate.

8
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Publish useful, timely material when ready.
A new topic does not reset an author-ID count.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Your best interval, the live settings and
the next post's reach remain unknown.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000
One Article passed 3K impressions after a week;
other Posts had hundreds, the author reports.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The review keeps that observation and explains why
it does not establish an advantage caused by format.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Use a Post for one question in a few paragraphs.
Use an Article for sections, figures and later reference.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Get a revised opening, length review, format advice
and a concrete first-image plan, with evidence limits.

14
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,500
Ask about posting frequency, links, images,
ranking claims, drafts or reach.

15
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:18,000
Install x-assistant and ask in your own words.
Find For You Skills on GitHub: alexliyu7352/for-you-skills.
